%% Bunny OS Phase 1 — Diagram 5 (file 10): Intent to Execution
%% One ordinary action traced from user expression to verified completion and
%% memory write-back. Draft classification is advisory. The fresh admission
%% evaluation and the adapter's receipt/hash/epoch validation are enforcing checks (§12.1, I6).

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as User
    participant SH as Bunny Shell
    participant BR as Bunny Broker
    participant IS as Intent Service
    participant PE as Plan Engine
    participant MEM as Memory Service
    participant CR as Capability Router
    participant POL as Policy Engine
    participant GL as Grant Ledger
    participant EC as Execution Controller
    participant URS as Update and Recovery Service
    participant SM as Sandbox Manager
    participant SBX as Sandbox
    participant AUD as Audit Service
    participant J as Durable Event Journal

    U->>SH: "get this project ready for release"
    SH->>BR: authenticated intent submission
    BR->>IS: normalized input (origin: user)
    IS->>IS: resolve to structured intent
    IS->>AUD: intent captured
    IS->>PE: accepted intent

    PE->>MEM: scoped retrieval request (workspace)
    MEM-->>PE: records + provenance + confidence
    Note over MEM,PE: only this workspace's scope —<br/>promotion requires consent

    PE->>CR: route request (task class, sensitivity, plan length)
    CR->>CR: evaluate posture, hardware, cost, health
    CR-->>PE: route decision + explanation record
    CR->>AUD: routing decision

    PE->>PE: draft living plan v1<br/>with immutable ActionSpecs
    PE->>POL: evaluate plan envelope and exact effects
    POL->>POL: classify each step by action class + disposition
    POL-->>BR: classes 1-5 are policy candidates<br/>step 6 requires a user grant
    BR->>GL: createRequest(step 6 ActionSpec,<br/>effect + plan hashes + rendered digest)
    GL-->>BR: request id + expected version + digest
    BR->>SH: plan proposal + displayed permission request
    SH->>U: review plan and exact external effect
    U->>SH: approve plan and request
    SH->>BR: authenticated plan approval +<br/>request-bound decision
    BR->>PE: approve graph sequence/hash
    BR->>GL: recordDecision(request id,<br/>expected version, displayed digest)
    GL->>GL: compare-and-swap and issue user grant
    GL->>J: append decision + GrantIssued + outbox
    J-->>AUD: committed authorization event

    loop each ready step
        PE->>EC: execute immutable ActionSpec
        EC->>URS: create recovery point if consequential
        URS-->>EC: durable recovery-point reference
        EC->>SM: prepare sandbox with no usable capability
        SM->>SBX: create with exact profile
        Note over SM,SBX: mounts, process limits,<br/>default-deny egress, no secrets
        EC->>POL: evaluateForAdmission(exact operation tuple,<br/>current authoritative context and epochs)
        POL-->>EC: fresh AdmissionEvaluation<br/>deny, user-grant-required, or policy-permit
        EC->>GL: prepare matching user reservation<br/>or policy authorization mutation
        GL-->>EC: owner-authorized mutation
        EC->>AUD: prepare AuditStart mutation
        AUD-->>EC: owner-authorized mutation
        EC->>J: admitEffect batch<br/>(authorization + ExecutionStarted + AuditStart)
        J-->>EC: all owner events + outbox fsynced
        Note over EC,J: only now may a usable capability exist
        EC->>SM: present admission receipt,<br/>exact ActionSpec and current epochs
        SM->>SM: independently validate receipt,<br/>ActionSpec hash and epochs
        SM->>SBX: materialize exact capability and execute ActionSpec
        SBX-->>EC: observations
        EC->>EC: verify — did this actually succeed?
        EC->>GL: prepare matching reservation terminal
        GL-->>EC: owner-authorized terminal mutation
        EC->>AUD: prepare AuditTerminal + egress mutation
        AUD-->>EC: owner-authorized terminal mutation
        EC->>J: finalizeEffect batch<br/>(Grant + Execution + Audit terminal)
        J-->>EC: atomic terminal receipt
        EC-->>PE: step verified
        PE->>SH: step state (streamed)
    end

    PE->>SH: plan complete + result review
    SH->>U: what was done, spent, sent, and what is undoable
    PE->>MEM: propose candidate memories
    Note over PE,MEM: proposals only — C8 forbids<br/>silent durable writes
    U->>SH: confirm memory proposals
    SH->>MEM: write (attributed, scoped, provenance)
    MEM->>AUD: memory write
